  "interpretation": [
    "The later completed raw-image backup supersedes the earlier audit statement that active system and critical partitions had not been backed up.",
    "The earlier inactive system_a hash covered the manifest-sized 5 GiB prefix, while the later raw backup covers the full 12,437,225,472-byte partition; these hashes are not directly comparable.",
    "Both historical system partitions and boot/firmware logical units were captured, but userdata and cache were not preserved as complete block images. Selected software/configuration archives exclude recordings, logs and transient data.",
    "Initial software/configuration tar had changed-file warnings. The subsequent 182-file configuration check passed but remained non-atomic.",
    "The old AGNOS image URL checks were historical HTTP availability only. They are not proof of current availability, a locally cached exact C3XL factory image or compatible recovery loader.",
    "The later SP2027 factory package is a different inspected application package (0.10.1, declared AGNOS 12.4 and Panda DEV-b0cd5291-RELEASE), not proof of an exact restore path for the current SP098 installation.",
    "USB gadget configuration and a UDC in Linux do not establish a physically accessible recovery port, EDL/fastboot operation, or a compatible loader.",
    "Running application, saved bootstub files, MCU contents, and provisioning are distinct evidence layers."
  ],
